  "query_preview": "(Today through Wednesday)...\nIssued at 304 AM EST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nToday through Friday...\n\nLatest satellite imagery depicts extensive low clouds persisting \nacross Indiana with considerable clearing noted across southern \nportions of Illinois. This clearing is associated with dry air \nadvection which will help to eventually clear out clouds across \nmuch of the area this morning. The clearing is only expected to \nbe brief as a weakening low pressure system and parent trough \napproach later in the day. \n\nModest moisture advection from the approaching system will quickly \nfilter in extensive low clouds during the afternoon hours. Weak \nforcing from the aforementioned features and an associated cold \nfront are also likely to promote scattered showers or drizzle this \nevening into the overnight hours. Cooler 850mb temperatures combined \nwith low clouds filtering in will keep temperatures about 10 \ndegrees cooler than yesterday. Look for highs to generally range \nfrom the mid 50s to low 60s.\n\nExtensive low clouds are likely to persist through the overnight \ninto Friday morning as guidance suggest the aforementioned cold \nfront does not move through until very late tonight. Cold air \nadvection behind the front will help to cool temperatures into the \nlow-mid 40s despite the clouds. At least partial clearing is \nexpected during the day Friday once drier air begins to filter in. \nHowever, scattered to broken low clouds should persist for much of \nthe day aided by lake enhanced low-level moisture. Limited diurnal \non top of continued cold air advection will keep highs in the low-\nmid 50s. A few lake enhanced showers or patchy drizzle cannot be \nruled out, mainly across far northern counties.\n\nFriday night through the middle of next week...\n\nQuiet weather conditions are expected towards the end of this week \nthrough the middle of next week as surface high pressure generally \nremains in control. Ensemble guidance depicts a few subtle systems \npushing weak cold fronts through the region. Gulf moisture remaining \ncutoff will keep these fronts moisture starved allowing for dry \nconditions to persist. Look for highs to remain in the 50s over the \nweekend before moderating back into the 60s early next week. \nMeanwhile, it appears Friday night through Sunday night will feature \nnear or sub-freezing lows across portions of central Indiana. Cloud \ncover leads to some uncertainty in forecasted lows, primarily Friday \nnight.",
